RETAIN STORAGE AND RECOVERY BOUNDARIES
Immutable StoreV2 profile 1 retains the 232-byte MSS2 record and generation zero.
AppendStoreV2 profile 2 retains the 280-byte MSU2 envelope, which wraps unchanged
MSS2 metadata with a local generation and checksum. MNM2, MRB2, MCF2 and prior
fixtures remain frozen. Generation starts at zero at any initialized height,
advances once per published child and never exceeds height. It is neither branch
weight nor global freshness. Independent network, complete checkpoint and
generation pins remain mandatory on reopening.

Kernel locks attach to the stable root inode: exclusive writers and shared
inspectors. Roots and parent directories are trusted, and all processes must
cooperate. There is no PID takeover, root replacement or explicit-unlock shortcut.
Inherited fork descriptors can prolong locks. Preserve process-test isolation and
do not hide ownership failures with retries. WSL, DrvFS, native Windows and network
mounts remain unverified by Ubuntu CI.

Append validates the complete child and replays the selected disk history. It
synchronizes the block and its directory, prepares the pending selector, compares
the old selection, renames the selector and synchronizes the root before memory
advances. Disk discrepancies and mutation failures fence normal access and further
writes. last_confirmed_checkpoint describes prior confirmed memory only. Clean
reconciliation and opening fully replay and resynchronize selected history, and
reject all staging.

MB-03C's explicit AppendRecoveryRequestV2 independently retains the parent and
candidate checkpoints and exact child, with adjacent heights and generations.
recover_interrupted acquires ownership of an existing root. Consuming recover
keeps the same lock, accepts an ordinary or fenced writer, and requires its last
confirmed checkpoint to match one endpoint. Every error returns no handle.
Fully replay the parent and validate the child before either recovery action.

Complete fills missing canonical suffixes and publishes the candidate. RetainParent
removes only matching authorized pending selection and then the unselected tail,
with root and blocks-directory synchronization in the specified order. Retention
is permitted only while the parent remains selected. An already selected candidate
supports idempotent Complete and cannot be rolled back.

A pending selector requires the full candidate child. A selected child requires
clean complete history without a pending selector. Unknown or non-prefix data,
unsafe aliases, and missing or corrupt selected history remain preserved and
rejected. Prefix equality does not prove file origin; the external request
authorizes only the named staging paths. There is no on-disk intent journal,
automatic repair, migration, or authority derived from checksums or the highest
generation.

Validated parent files are synchronized before mutation. Bytes, current file
identity and selection are rechecked. Strict final replay, complete ledger/counter
equality and resynchronization are required before a usable writer is returned.
RecoveryIncomplete and PublicationUncertain retain their documented meanings.
Arbitrary corruption, interrupted initialization and lost-intent recovery remain
unsupported. Distinct encoded recovery inputs are bounded to 19,559,412 bytes.
The conservative per-call payload-read allowance is 156,508,096 bytes, including
comparisons, sentinels and final replay. Preserve finite bounds and trusted-owner
assumptions. These are not RSS limits or unconditional crash-safety claims.

